{%- doc -%}
A reviews section modeled visually on the Okendo reviews widget (rating summary, a sort control, review
cards with reviewer/product/attribute info and an attribute bar), but built natively with theme blocks
instead of depending on the Okendo app.

Reviews are not stored anywhere outside the theme: each review shown on the storefront is a "Review"
block that the merchant adds/edits/reorders from the theme editor, exactly like the FAQ block. Only the
first 5 review cards show initially; a "Ver más" button reveals 5 more at a time, and disappears once
every review is visible. Sorting always re-applies before the reveal count, so changing sort resets back
to the first 5 of the newly sorted order.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign review_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'review'

  # Same metafields snippets/product-rating.liquid already reads (product.metafields.custom.reviews_rating
  # / reviews_count) - when this section sits on a product page and they're set, the summary badge shown
  # here matches whatever the product card/product page already shows, instead of only reflecting however
  # many "Review" blocks happen to be added below. Falls back to counting/averaging the blocks themselves
  # when the metafields aren't set (eg. a non-product page, or a product without them yet).
  if product and product.metafields.custom.reviews_rating.value != blank
    assign average_rating = product.metafields.custom.reviews_rating.value.rating | plus: 0 | round: 1
    assign review_count = product.metafields.custom.reviews_count.value | default: 0
  else
    assign review_count = review_blocks.size
    assign rating_sum = 0

    for review_block in review_blocks
      assign rating_sum = rating_sum | plus: review_block.settings.rating
    endfor

    if review_count > 0
      assign average_rating = rating_sum | times: 1.0 | divided_by: review_count | round: 1
    else
      assign average_rating = 0
    endif
  endif

  assign write_review_modal_id = 'write-review-' | append: section.id

  # "Escribir una reseña" (the button and the popup it opens) only exists once the merchant adds
  # this block - same opt-in pattern as any other singleton block (eg. main-cart's "totals") - so
  # there's one place to configure the popup (color scheme, centering, radius...) instead of those
  # settings floating at the section level disconnected from what they control.
  assign write_review_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'write_review_popup' | first
-%}

{%- comment -%}
Google can read these reviews (setting "Let Google read these reviews"): on a product page the average and the reviews are handed to
layout/theme.liquid, which merges them into the product's structured data (snippets/microdata-schema.liquid) as aggregateRating and
review. They travel as a hidden HTML comment, because the layout renders the page head before this section exists. Only the reviews the
visitor can read on the page are included, with the same average and count shown in the summary.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if section.settings.reviews_structured_data and request.page_type == 'product' and review_count > 0 -%}
  {%- assign reviews_ld_printed = 0 -%}
  {%- capture reviews_ld -%}
    "aggregateRating": {
      "@type": "AggregateRating",
      "ratingValue": {{ average_rating | json }},
      "reviewCount": {{ review_count | json }},
      "bestRating": 5,
      "worstRating": 1
    },
    "review": [
      {%- for review_block in review_blocks -%}
        {%- if review_block.settings.reviewer_name != blank and review_block.settings.rating > 0 -%}
          {%- assign reviews_ld_printed = reviews_ld_printed | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- if reviews_ld_printed > 1 -%},{%- endif -%}
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": {{ review_block.settings.reviewer_name | json }} },
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": {{ review_block.settings.rating | json }},
              "bestRating": 5,
              "worstRating": 1
            }
            {%- if review_block.settings.title != blank -%},
            "name": {{ review_block.settings.title | strip_html | json }}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if review_block.settings.body != blank -%},
            "reviewBody": {{ review_block.settings.body | strip_html | strip | json }}
            {%- endif -%}
          }
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {{- '<!--reviews-ld:' -}}{{- reviews_ld | strip_newlines | remove: '-->' -}}{{- ':reviews-ld-->' -}}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
The reviews (name, stars and text) for the Instagram Feed's zoom view (sections/instagram-feed.liquid shows them, one at a time, over the video): a hidden
block of data on the page, read by that section when a video is opened. It holds only what the visitor can already read here. The text is complete:
the zoom view shortens it to two lines by itself and offers "Ver más".
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if review_blocks.size > 0 -%}
  {%- assign lightbox_reviews_printed = 0 -%}
  <script type="application/json" data-reviews-lightbox>
    [
      {%- for review_block in review_blocks -%}
        {%- assign lightbox_review_text = review_block.settings.body | strip_html | strip -%}

        {%- if lightbox_review_text == blank -%}
          {%- assign lightbox_review_text = review_block.settings.title | strip_html | strip -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- capture lightbox_review_date_result -%}{%- render 'review-date', index: forloop.index -%}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- assign lightbox_review_date = lightbox_review_date_result | strip | split: '|' | last -%}

        {%- if lightbox_review_text != blank -%}
          {%- assign lightbox_reviews_printed = lightbox_reviews_printed | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- if lightbox_reviews_printed > 1 -%},{%- endif -%}
          { "name": {{ review_block.settings.reviewer_name | json }}, "rating": {{ review_block.settings.rating | default: 0 | json }}, "date": {{ lightbox_review_date | json }}, "text": {{ lightbox_review_text | json }} }
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

<div class="color-scheme color-scheme--{{ section.settings.color_scheme.id }}{% if section.settings.floating_reviews %} section-floating section-floating--block{% endif %}"{% if section.settings.floating_reviews %} style="border-radius: {{ section.settings.reviews_border_radius }}px; overflow: hidden;"{% endif %}>
  <div class="section-spacing">
    <div id="reviews-{{ section.id }}" class="reviews section-stack">
        <div class="reviews__summary-row">
          <div class="reviews__summary">
            <div class="reviews__summary-rating">
              <span class="reviews__summary-average"><span class="reviews__summary-average-number {{ section.settings.heading_size }}">{{ average_rating }}</span></span>

              <div class="reviews__summary-stars-column">
                <span class="reviews__stars" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'general.rating.info' | t: rating_value: average_rating, rating_max: 5 }}">
                  {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign half_threshold = i | minus: 0.5

                      if review_count == 0
                        render 'icon' with 'star-rating-empty'
                      elsif average_rating >= i
                        render 'icon' with 'star-rating'
                      elsif average_rating >= half_threshold
                        render 'icon' with 'star-rating-half'
                      else
                        render 'icon' with 'star-rating-empty'
                      endif
                    -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </span>

                <p class="reviews__summary-count">Basado en {{ review_count }} reseña{% if review_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
        Phone only: the "Escribir una reseña" button is replaced by a full-width box like the one in the zoom view of the Instagram Feed (picture, the
        field and a send button once there is text). Sending opens the same window the button opens, with the text already in the review field.
        The button stays in the page (hidden on phones) because the window is opened through it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if write_review_block != blank and review_blocks.size > 0 -%}
          <form class="reviews__compose" data-reviews-compose autocomplete="off">
            <span class="reviews__compose-avatar" data-review-avatar=""></span>
            <input type="text" class="reviews__compose-input" placeholder="Escribe una reseña" aria-label="Escribe una reseña" enterkeyhint="send">
            <button type="submit" class="reviews__compose-send" hidden>Enviar</button>
          </form>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if review_blocks.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="reviews__controls">
            {%- if write_review_block != blank -%}
              <div class="reviews__summary-write">
                {%- render 'button', content: 'Escribir una reseña', aria_controls: write_review_modal_id, class: 'reviews__write-button' -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="reviews__sort button">
              <label class="sr-only" for="reviews-sort-{{ section.id }}">Sort reviews</label>
              <div class="button__content">
                <select id="reviews-sort-{{ section.id }}" class="select" data-reviews-sort>
                  <option value="rating_desc" selected>Highest rated</option>
                  <option value="recent">Most recent</option>
                  <option value="rating_asc">Lowest rated</option>
                </select>
                {%- render 'icon' with 'chevron-down' -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="reviews__list" data-reviews-list>
            {%- for block in review_blocks -%}
              {%- comment -%}
              Date shown per review is computed, not merchant-entered (block.settings.date_label is
              no longer read) - it auto-advances once every 24 hours (day_count, from the current
              unix timestamp, is the same integer for everyone until the next UTC day) and never
              reads as fresher than ~4-6 days or older than ~2 months: review_date_days cycles
              through that [4, 59] range, wrapping back to the start every 56 days instead of
              counting up forever. Each review gets a different point in that same cycle (seeded off
              forloop.index) so they don't all display the exact same age on a given day.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- capture review_date_result -%}{%- render 'review-date', index: forloop.index -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- assign review_date_parts = review_date_result | strip | split: '|' -%}
              {%- assign review_date_days = review_date_parts[0] -%}
              {%- assign review_date_label = review_date_parts[1] -%}
              <div class="review-card" data-review-id="{{ block.id }}" data-rating="{{ block.settings.rating }}" data-days-ago="{{ review_date_days }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <div class="review-card__side">
                  <div class="review-card__reviewer">
                    <span class="review-card__avatar" data-review-avatar="{{ block.settings.reviewer_name | escape }}"></span>
                    <div class="review-card__identity">
                      <div class="review-card__name-row">
                        <span class="review-card__name">{{ block.settings.reviewer_name }}</span>

                        {%- if block.settings.verified_buyer -%}
                          <span class="review-card__verified">
                            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" class="review-card__verified-badge"><path d="M12.00 2.00 L15.21 4.24 L19.07 4.93 L19.76 8.79 L22.00 12.00 L19.76 15.21 L19.07 19.07 L15.21 19.76 L12.00 22.00 L8.79 19.76 L4.93 19.07 L4.24 15.21 L2.00 12.00 L4.24 8.79 L4.93 4.93 L8.79 4.24Z" fill="#0095f6" stroke="#0095f6" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="m7.9 12.2 2.9 2.9 5.4-5.8" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                            <span class="sr-only">Comprador verificado</span>
                          </span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </div>

                      <span class="review-card__handle" data-review-handle="{{ block.settings.reviewer_name | escape }}"></span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="review-card__main">
                  <div class="review-card__top">
                    <span class="review-card__stars" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'general.rating.info' | t: rating_value: block.settings.rating, rating_max: 5 }}">
                      {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
                        {%- liquid
                          assign half_threshold = i | minus: 0.5

                          if block.settings.rating >= i
                            render 'icon' with 'star-rating'
                          elsif block.settings.rating >= half_threshold
                            render 'icon' with 'star-rating-half'
                          else
                            render 'icon' with 'star-rating-empty'
                          endif
                        -%}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </span>

                    <span class="review-card__date">{{ review_date_label }}</span>
                  </div>

                  {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
                    <p class="review-card__title">{{ block.settings.title }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}

                  {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
                    <div class="review-card__body">
                      {{- block.settings.body -}}
                    </div>
                  {%- endif -%}

                  {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
                    <div class="review-card__image">
                      {{- block.settings.image | image_url: width: block.settings.image.width | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '120px', widths: '120,240,360' -}}
                    </div>
                  {%- endif -%}

                  <div class="review-card__actions">
                    <button type="button" class="review-card__like" aria-pressed="false" data-review-like>
                      <span class="sr-only">Me gusta</span>
                      {%- render 'icon' with 'heart' -%}
                      <span class="review-card__like-count" aria-live="polite"></span>
                    </button>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if review_blocks.size > 1 -%}
          <div class="reviews__load-more">
            {%- render 'button', content: 'Ver más', type: 'button', style: 'outline', class: 'reviews__load-more-button' -%}
            {%- render 'button', content: 'Ver menos', type: 'button', style: 'outline', class: 'reviews__load-less-button' -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- if write_review_block != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
  The form block has to run (and "form" become available) before the has_form_feedback check below, so its
  output is captured here and echoed inside the modal afterwards - not evaluated directly inside the
  <x-modal> tag, whose opening tag (with the "open" attribute) needs that same check to happen first.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture review_form_content -%}
    {%- form 'contact', class: 'form' -%}
      {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
        {%- render 'banner', status: 'success', content: '¡Gracias! Tu reseña fue enviada y aparecerá aquí una vez aprobada.' -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if form.errors -%}
        {%- capture error_content -%}{{ form.errors.translated_fields[form.errors.first] | capitalize }} {{ form.errors.messages[form.errors.first] }}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- render 'banner', status: 'error', content: error_content -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}Once the review is sent only the confirmation stays, instead of an empty form inviting a second submission.{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- unless form.posted_successfully? -%}
      {%- comment -%}Kept after a failed submission; otherwise the signed-in customer's own data. (render tags cannot apply filters inline.){%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign review_name = form.name | default: customer.name -%}
      {%- assign review_email = form.email | default: customer.email -%}

      <input type="hidden" name="contact[Submission type]" value="Review">

      <p class="review-form__required-note">Los campos marcados con * son obligatorios.</p>

      <fieldset class="review-form__rating">
        <legend class="review-form__rating-label">¿Cómo calificarías tu experiencia? <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></legend>
        <div class="review-form__star-picker">
          {%- for i in (1..5) reversed -%}
            {%- capture rating_id -%}review-rating-{{ i }}-{{ section.id }}{%- endcapture -%}
            <input type="radio" name="contact[Rating]" id="{{ rating_id }}" value="{{ i }}" required>
            <label for="{{ rating_id }}">
              <span class="sr-only">{{ i }} estrella{% if i != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span>
              {%- comment -%}Same rounded star as the rating icons (snippets/icon.liquid, 'star-rating'){%- endcomment -%}
              <svg viewBox="0.996 0.786 11.008 11.008" overflow="visible" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" width="26" height="26">
                <path d="M7.124 1.795 L7.943 4.151 Q8.107 4.623 8.607 4.633 L11.1 4.684 Q13 4.723 11.486 5.871 L9.498 7.377 Q9.1 7.679 9.245 8.158 L9.967 10.545 Q10.517 12.364 8.958 11.279 L6.91 9.854 Q6.5 9.568 6.09 9.854 L4.042 11.279 Q2.483 12.364 3.033 10.545 L3.755 8.158 Q3.9 7.679 3.502 7.377 L1.514 5.871 Q0 4.723 1.9 4.684 L4.393 4.633 Q4.893 4.623 5.057 4.151 L5.876 1.795 Q6.5 0 7.124 1.795Z" stroke-width=".6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </label>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="fieldset">
        {%- comment -%}
        The product the customer bought, picked from the store's available products (the first 50 the store lists - a loop over a collection
        stops there). On a product page that product is already selected.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture review_product_options -%}
          <option value="" disabled{% unless product %} selected{% endunless %}>Elige el producto que compraste</option>
          {%- for review_product in collections.all.products limit: 50 -%}
            {%- if review_product.available or review_product.id == product.id -%}
              <option value="{{ review_product.title | escape }}"{% if review_product.id == product.id %} selected{% endif %}>{{ review_product.title | escape }}</option>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}

        {%- render 'select', options: review_product_options, name: 'contact[Producto]', label: 'Producto que compraste', show_label_as_block: true, required: true, id_prefix: 'review-product' -%}

        {%- render 'input', type: 'text', name: 'contact[Review title]', label: 'Agregar un título', show_label_as_block: true, placeholder: 'Resume tu experiencia en una frase', required: true, maxlength: 80 -%}
        {%- render 'input', name: 'contact[body]', label: 'Escribe una reseña', show_label_as_block: true, placeholder: 'Cuéntanos cómo fue tu experiencia y qué resultados notaste.', multiline: 5, required: true, minlength: 10, maxlength: 1500, show_max_characters_count: true -%}

        {%- comment -%}
        The same details every published review shows next to its text (skin type, age, main concern, previous
        peel experience), all optional. The product is chosen above, in its own field.
        Option lists are split from a comma separated string, so no option may contain a comma.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign review_skin_types = 'Normal,Mixta,Grasa,Seca,Sensible' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- assign review_ages = '18 - 24,25 - 34,35 - 44,45 - 54,55 o más' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- assign review_concerns = 'Textura irregular,Manchas,Poros dilatados,Opacidad,Cicatrices de acné,Arrugas,Otra' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- assign review_experiences = 'Primera vez,Ya lo había probado antes' | split: ',' -%}

        <p class="review-form__section-note">Cuéntanos sobre ti (opcional). Así ayudas a quienes tienen tu mismo tipo de piel.</p>

        <div class="fieldset-row">
          {%- render 'select', option_values: review_skin_types, show_empty_value: true, name: 'contact[Tipo de piel]', label: 'Tipo de piel' -%}
          {%- render 'select', option_values: review_ages, show_empty_value: true, name: 'contact[Edad]', label: 'Edad' -%}
        </div>

        <div class="fieldset-row">
          {%- render 'select', option_values: review_concerns, show_empty_value: true, name: 'contact[Preocupación principal]', label: 'Preocupación principal' -%}
          {%- render 'select', option_values: review_experiences, show_empty_value: true, name: 'contact[Experiencia previa con peelings]', label: 'Experiencia previa con peelings' -%}
        </div>

        <div class="fieldset-row">
          {%- render 'input', type: 'text', name: 'contact[name]', label: 'Nombre', value: review_name, required: true, autocomplete: 'name', maxlength: 60 -%}
          {%- render 'input', type: 'email', name: 'contact[email]', label: 'Correo electrónico', value: review_email, required: true, autocomplete: 'email' -%}
        </div>

        <p class="review-form__privacy-note">Tu correo no se publicará.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="review-form__submit">
        {%- render 'button', content: 'Enviar reseña', type: 'submit', class: 'sm-max:w-full' -%}
      </div>
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endform -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- liquid
    assign has_form_feedback = false

    if form.posted_successfully? or form.errors
      assign has_form_feedback = true
    endif
  -%}

  <x-modal id="{{ write_review_modal_id }}" append-to-body {% if has_form_feedback %}open{% endif %} class="modal modal--lg modal--write-review color-scheme color-scheme--{{ write_review_block.settings.color_scheme.id }}" {{ write_review_block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- comment -%}
    The title stays pinned at the top (with the close button, which is positioned against the popup itself) and only
    the form scrolls: the header is a normal block outside the scrolling area, see ".review-modal__scroll" below.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if write_review_block.settings.title != blank or write_review_block.settings.subtitle != blank -%}
      <div class="review-modal__header prose">
        {%- if write_review_block.settings.title != blank -%}
          <p class="h4">{{ write_review_block.settings.title }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if write_review_block.settings.subtitle != blank -%}
          <p class="review-modal__subtitle">{{ write_review_block.settings.subtitle }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="review-modal__scroll">
      {{- review_form_content -}}
    </div>
  </x-modal>

  <style>
    {%- comment -%}
    append-to-body (above) moves this modal out to <body> at runtime, outside
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} - so this is scoped by the modal's own id instead, which stays
    valid wherever it ends up in the DOM. modal--lg (theme.css) gives it a wider, more usable content
    column instead of the base .modal's 30rem cap, which read cramped for a form this long (star
    picker, title, review body, name/email).

    place-self/width below mirror sections/newsletter-popup.liquid's own "Center popup" and
    "Ancho en móvil" settings exactly (including leaving the mobile bottom-sheet default alone unless
    a narrower width is explicitly chosen) - same popup system, same two settings, instead of a
    separate one-off implementation here.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
    The body part normally scrolls as a whole; here the form scrolls on its own (.review-modal__scroll) so the header
    and the close button stay put. The header reserves room at its end for the close button.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
    Inner padding: the same one every floating container uses (container gutter + 0.5rem), at every width, instead of
    the generic modal's fixed 1.25rem / 3rem. The ID selector beats .modal's own values for these variables.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #{{ write_review_modal_id }}.modal--write-review {
      --modal-body-padding-block: calc(var(--container-gutter) + 0.5rem);
      --modal-body-padding-inline: calc(var(--container-gutter) + 0.5rem);
    }

    #{{ write_review_modal_id }}.modal--write-review::part(body) {
      overflow: hidden;
      grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: stretch;
      align-content: start;
    }

    #{{ write_review_modal_id }} .review-modal__header {
      padding-inline-end: 2.5rem;
      padding-block-end: 1.25rem;
    }

    #{{ write_review_modal_id }} .review-modal__header p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    #{{ write_review_modal_id }} .review-modal__subtitle {
      margin-block-start: .5rem;
      color: rgb(var(--text-color) / .7);
    }

    #{{ write_review_modal_id }} .review-modal__scroll {
      min-height: 0;
      overflow-y: auto;
      overscroll-behavior-y: contain;
      padding: .25rem;
      margin: -.25rem;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    Full height: the popup takes all the height of the screen (the generic modal caps it at 70vh), minus the modal's own margin
    (--modal-content-margin) above and below, so it keeps the same gap to the screen's edge on every side.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #{{ write_review_modal_id }}.modal--write-review::part(content) {
      height: calc(100vh - 2 * var(--modal-content-margin));
      max-height: none;
      border-radius: {{ write_review_block.settings.popup_border_radius }}px;
      overflow: hidden;
      {%- if write_review_block.settings.center_popup -%}
        place-self: center;
      {%- endif -%}
    }

    @supports (height: 100dvh) {
      #{{ write_review_modal_id }}.modal--write-review::part(content) {
